"In a clothing store, 40 white shirts and 50 floral shirts are held. Half of the white shirts are collared, and buttons are featured on 20 of the floral shirts. How many more floral shirts with no buttons are there than white shirts with no collars?","A clothing store has 40 white shirts and 50 floral shirts. Half of the white shirts have collars, and 20 of the floral shirts have buttons. How many more floral shirts with no buttons are there than white shirts with no collars?",10,10,10,10,"Step 1: Identify totals.
- White shirts: 40
- Floral shirts: 50

Step 2: Determine white shirts with no collars.
- Half of white shirts are collared → collared white = 40/2 = 20
- No-collar white = 40 − 20 = 20

Step 3: Determine floral shirts with no buttons.
- Buttons on floral shirts = 20
- No-button floral = 50 − 20 = 30

Step 4: Find how many more no-button floral than no-collar white.
- 30 − 20 = 10

####10",,"Step 1: Identify totals.
- White shirts: 40
- Floral shirts: 50
Step 2: Determine white shirts with no collars.
