"A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 10 minutes for every 3 miles of the city to be covered. If the city is 42 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the whole city to be covered by the fog bank?","A fog bank rolls in from the ocean to cover a city. It takes 10 minutes to cover every 3 miles of the city. If the city is 42 miles across from the oceanfront to the opposite inland edge, how many minutes will it take for the fog bank to cover the whole city?",140,140,140,140,"Step 1: Identify the rate of coverage.
