"Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Each mile was run twice as fast by Aaron as by Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If 4 miles were run by Vanessa and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?","Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?",64,64,64,64,"Let’s define variables:
- Let v be Vanessa’s running rate in miles per minute.
- Then Aaron’s rate is 2v (since Aaron is twice as fast per mile).

Distances:
- Vanessa ran 4 miles.
- Vanessa ran twice as far as Aaron, so Aaron ran 2 miles.

Times:
- Aaron’s time = distance / rate = 2 miles / (2v) = 1/v minutes.
- We’re told Aaron completed his part in 16 minutes, so 1/v = 16 ⇒ v = 1/16 miles per minute.

Vanessa’s time:
- Time = distance / rate = 4 miles / (1/16) = 4 × 16 = 64 minutes.

