"The number of students in a school hall was 1000. The hall had 3 entrances A, B, and C which also served as the exits. If after a meeting 30% of the students were seen exiting the building through exit A, 3/5 of the remaining were observed exiting through exit B, and the rest were seen exiting through exit C, calculate the number of students who went out through exit C.","The number of students in a school hall was 1000. The hall had 3 entrances A, B, and C which also served as the exits. If after a meeting 30% of the students went out of the building through exit A, 3/5 of the remaining went out through exit B, and the rest went out through exit C, calculate the number of students who went out through exit C.",280,280,280,280,"Step 1: Total students = 1000.

Step 2: Exiting through A = 30% of 1000 = 0.30 × 1000 = 300.
Remaining after A = 1000 − 300 = 700.

Step 3: Exiting through B = 3/5 of remaining = (3/5) × 700 = 420.
Remaining after B = 700 − 420 = 280.

Step 4: Those exiting through C are the remaining students = 280.

