John hires a driving service to get him to work each day. His work is 30 miles away and he has to go there and back each day. He goes to work 5 days a week for 50 weeks a year. He gets charged $2 per mile driven and he also gives his driver a $150 bonus per month. How much is paid by him a year for driving?,John hires a driving service to get him to work each day. His work is 30 miles away and he has to go there and back each day. He goes to work 5 days a week for 50 weeks a year. He gets charged $2 per mile driven and he also gives his driver a $150 bonus per month. How much does he pay a year for driving?,31800,31800,318,318,"Step 1: Determine daily miles.
- One-way distance: 30 miles
- Round trip per day: 30 × 2 = 60 miles

Step 2: Determine annual miles.
- Workdays per week: 5
- Weeks per year: 50
- Total workdays per year: 5 × 50 = 250
- Annual miles: 60 × 250 = 15,000 miles

Step 3: Calculate mileage cost.
- Cost per mile: $2
- Mileage cost per year: 15,000 × 2 = $30,000

Step 4: Calculate annual bonus.
- Monthly bonus: $150
- Months per year: 12
- Annual bonus: 150 × 12 = $1,800

Step 5: Total annual cost.
- Total = Mileage cost + Annual bonus = 30,000 + 1,800 = $31,800

