"The Smith family is getting ready for summer and needs to have their swimming pool filled. Instructions were given by the pool company to measure to find the volume of the pool, then to multiply it by 5.9 to calculate how many gallons of water are needed. The cost for the pool company to come and fill the pool is $0.10 per gallon. The pool was measured by Mr. Smith and found to be 14 feet wide, 25 feet long, and 4 feet deep. How much will it cost to fill the pool?","The Smith family is getting ready for summer and needs to have their swimming pool filled. The pool company instructed them to measure to find the volume of the pool, then to multiply it by 5.9 to calculate how many gallons of water they need. The cost for the pool company to come and fill the pool is $0.10 per gallon. Mr. Smith measured and found the pool is 14 feet wide, 25 feet long, and 4 feet deep. How much will it cost to fill the pool?",826,826,826,826.00,"Step 1: Compute the volume of the pool (rectangular prism)
- Volume = length × width × depth = 25 ft × 14 ft × 4 ft = 1400 cubic feet

Step 2: Convert volume to gallons
- Given instruction: multiply cubic feet by 5.9 to get gallons
- Gallons = 1400 × 5.9 = 8260 gallons

Step 3: Compute the cost at $0.10 per gallon
- Cost = 8260 × $0.10 = $826.00

