"Bob has a certain number of marbles. If 2 dozen more marbles are received by him, he will have 60 marbles. If he loses 10 of the marbles he has, how many marbles will Bob have?","Bob has a certain number of marbles. If he receives 2 dozen more marbles, he will have 60 marbles. If he loses 10 of the marbles he has, how many marbles will Bob have?",26,26,26,26,"Let x be the number of marbles Bob initially has.

- “2 dozen more marbles are received by him” means he gets 24 more: x + 24 = 60
- Solve for x: x = 60 − 24 = 36

If he loses 10 of the marbles he has:
- New total = 36 − 10 = 26

